{# goal: Deterministically serialize the validated sourced edge array into Mermaid Sankey CSV and surface it as the process's final markdown output. #}
{# Format and surface the validated Sankey edge array as the process's final output.
   This is a pure Jinja2 template (the [inference] header carries only the render contract; no LLM call) rendered by
   the `render_template` tool from the SKILL.md body's final step. It wraps the
   adapt step's notes and the original sourced edges in a titled, annotated document with:
   - A title derived from domain + subject
   - A description paragraph (domain, weight unit, conservation mode, ontology)
   - A Mermaid sankey-beta diagram serialized directly from edges
   - A flow annotation table (source → target, weight, provenance)
   - A conservation check line
   - A notes section (CSV-unsafe IDs, placeholders, structural deviations)
   - An output path for file save

   Deterministic — no LLM call. All formatting is Jinja2 template logic. #}
[inference]
contract:
  input:
    subject: string
    domain: string
    weight_unit: string
    conservation_mode: string
    conservation_check: string
    nodes: array
    edges: array
    adapt_notes:
      type: string
      required: false
    output_path:
      type: string
      required: false
  output:
    markdown: string
---

{# ── Title ── #}
{%- set domain_title = domain | replace("-", " ") | title -%}
{%- set subject_title = subject | replace("-", " ") | title -%}

# {{ domain_title }}: {{ subject_title }}

{# ── Description ── #}

This diagram visualizes a {{ domain | replace("-", " ") }} flow with {{ nodes | length }} nodes and {{ edges | length }} edges. Measured weights are in {{ weight_unit }}; any `value=1` placeholders are unitless and named in the flow annotations. Conservation mode: **{{ conservation_mode }}**{% if conservation_mode == "mandatory" %} — each internal node requires an observed inflow/outflow check; see status below.{% elif conservation_mode == "asserted" %} — report observed discrepancies; enforce only if the user requires conservation.{% elif conservation_mode == "none" %} — conservation is skipped; do not invent balancing branches.{% endif %}

{# ── Mermaid diagram ── #}

```mermaid
---
config:
  sankey:
    showValues: true
    width: 900
    height: 500
    linkColor: source
---
sankey-beta
%% source,target,value
{%- for edge in edges %}
{{ edge.source }},{{ edge.target }},{{ edge.weight }}
{%- endfor %}
```

{# ── Flow annotations ── #}

| Source | Target | Weight | Notes |
|--------|--------|--------|-------|
{%- for edge in edges %}
| {{ edge.source }} | {{ edge.target }} | {{ edge.weight }} | {{ edge.weight_source | default("(not specified)") }} |
{%- endfor %}

{# ── Conservation check ── #}

**Conservation:** {{ conservation_check }}

{# ── Notes ── #}
{% if adapt_notes %}

**Notes:** {{ adapt_notes }}
{% endif %}

---

Output path: {{ output_path | default("docs/diagrams/sankey-" ~ domain ~ "-" ~ subject ~ ".md") }}
